{
  "id": "check-factorising-harder-quadratics-2",
  "title": "Check: Factorising Harder Quadratics",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Factorise $6x^2 + x - 2$.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$(3x + 2)(2x - 1)$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$(3x - 2)(2x + 1)$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$(6x - 1)(x + 2)$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$(2x + 1)(3x - 2)$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "We need factors of $6 \\times (-2) = -12$ that add to $1$: these are $4$ and $-3$. Splitting: $6x^2 + 4x - 3x - 2 = 2x(3x+2) - 1(3x+2) = (3x+2)(2x-1)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Factorise $4x^2 - 25$.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$(4x + 5)(x - 5)$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$(2x + 5)(2x - 5)$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$(2x - 5)^2$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$(4x - 5)(x + 5)$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "This is a difference of two squares: $4x^2 - 25 = (2x)^2 - 5^2 = (2x + 5)(2x - 5)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Factorise $5x^2 + 13x - 6$.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$(5x - 3)(x + 2)$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$(5x + 2)(x - 3)$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$(5x - 2)(x + 3)$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$(5x + 3)(x - 2)$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "We need factors of $5 \\times (-6) = -30$ that add to $13$: these are $15$ and $-2$. Splitting: $5x^2 + 15x - 2x - 6 = 5x(x+3) - 2(x+3) = (5x-2)(x+3)$."
    }
  ]
}
